      ⍝ Bugs38 #55: the nesting of a ⎕RE result is that of the groups in the
      ⍝ pattern (not of the spans of the match)





      2 ⎕TF 'Z'⊣Z←'(a(x)?)b' ⎕RE 'axb'
Z←2⍴'axb' (2⍴'ax' (1⍴'x'))




      2 ⎕TF 'Z'⊣Z←'(a(x)?)b' ⎕RE 'ab'
Z←2⍴'ab' (2⍴(1⍴'a') (''))




      2 ⎕TF 'Z'⊣Z←'(a(c?))b' ⎕RE 'ab'
Z←2⍴'ab' (2⍴(1⍴'a') (''))




      2 ⎕TF 'Z'⊣Z←'(?=(ab))(a)' ⎕RE 'ab'
Z←3⍴(1⍴'a') 'ab' (1⍴'a')




      2 ⎕TF 'Z'⊣Z←'(a(x)?)b' ⎕RE['↓'] 'ab'
Z←3⍴0 2 (3⍴0 1 (¯1 0))




      2 ⎕TF 'Z'⊣Z←'(a(b)?)?c' ⎕RE 'c'
Z←2⍴(1⍴'c') (2⍴('') (''))




      2 ⎕TF 'Z'⊣Z←'(\()(x)' ⎕RE '(x'
Z←3⍴'(x' (1⍴'(') (1⍴'x')




